---
import SeoHead from "../components/SeoHead.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { getCatalog, number, versionPath } from "../lib/plugin-details.mjs";
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { resolve } from "node:path";
const catalog = getCatalog();
const report = catalog.mediaReport;
const missing = Object.values(catalog.media.resources).filter((resource) => resource.status === "unavailable");
const releaseLookup = new Map([...catalog.projects.values()].flatMap((project) => project.releases.map((release) => [String(release.id), { project, release }])));
const methods = Object.values(catalog.media.resources).reduce((counts, row) => { if (row.method) counts[row.method] = (counts[row.method] || 0) + 1; return counts; }, {});
const recovery = JSON.parse(readFileSync(resolve("data/snapshots", catalog.pointer.snapshot_id, "media-recovery-audit.json"), "utf8"));
const chrome = JSON.parse(readFileSync(resolve("data/snapshots", catalog.pointer.snapshot_id, "media-chrome-audit.json"), "utf8"));
const recovered = Object.values(recovery.records).filter((row) => row.status === "preserved");
const scope = (row) => row.revision_verified ? "Original release source revision" : row.method === "wayback_capture" ? `Wayback capture ${row.wayback_timestamp}${row.capture_scope === "related_repository_url" ? "; related repository URL, release-time identity unverified" : row.capture_scope === "same_repository_other_revision" ? "; another repository revision" : ""}` : row.method === "verified_phar_entry" ? "Original PHAR entry; upstream image identity unverified" : "Other repository revision; original release image unverified";
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><SeoHead title="Preservation status - Poggit Archive" description="Preserved media, local documents, provenance and remaining external references in Poggit Archive." path="/preservation/" /><link rel="icon" href="/favicon-32x32.png"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css?v=theme-1"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/plugin-details.css?v=theme-1"></head><body>
<SiteHeader />
<main class="preservation-page"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Catalog</a><span>/</span><span>Preservation</span></nav><h1>Preservation status</h1><p>Plugin pages, images, fonts, descriptions and changelogs are served from this archive. Browsing the catalog does not require Poggit, the original repositories or external image hosts.</p>
<section class="detail-section"><h2>Preserved images</h2><p>Captured on {catalog.media.captured_at?.slice(0, 10)}. Release metadata and download counts remain those of the {catalog.pointer.captured_at.slice(0, 10)} snapshot.</p><dl class="compact-facts preservation-facts"><dt>Image contexts</dt><dd>{number(report.image_contexts)}</dd><dt>Preserved</dt><dd>{number(report.preserved)}</dd><dt>Snapshot labels</dt><dd>{number(report.reconstructed)}</dd><dt>Unavailable</dt><dd>{number(report.unavailable)}</dd><dt>Unique files</dt><dd>{number(report.unique_display_files)}</dd><dt>Image storage</dt><dd>{((report.display_bytes || 0) / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(1)} MiB</dd><dt>Release icons</dt><dd>{number(report.releases_with_preserved_icons)} / {number(report.release_icon_references)} recorded icons</dd></dl><p>Images from the plugin's own repository are pinned to its build commit when possible. Images extracted from a PHAR are tied to that PHAR's checksum. Dead Poggit badges are replaced by clearly marked snapshot labels, with separate reconstruction records. Other images and badges record their capture date; their contents may differ from the earlier release snapshot. SVG images are rasterized for display, with their captured source retained as plain text. Unavailable images use a local placeholder and never fall back to the original host.</p><details><summary>Capture methods</summary><pre>{JSON.stringify(methods, null, 2)}</pre></details><p><a class="text-link" href="/data/api/v1/media-mirror.json">Media manifest, source URLs and checksums</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/dependency-audit.json">Build dependency audit</a></p></section>
<section id="media-recovery" class="detail-section"><h2>Image recovery follow-up</h2><p>Of the {number(recovery.baseline_unavailable)} previously unavailable image contexts, {number(recovery.recovered)} now have a local image and {number(recovery.remaining)} remain unavailable. {number(recovery.release_revision_verified)} recovered contexts are tied to original release source revisions. Wayback captures retain their archive timestamps. Images found only in another revision are explicitly identified below and in their image tooltips.</p><p><a class="text-link" href={`/data/snapshots/${catalog.pointer.snapshot_id}/media-recovery-audit.json`}>Recovery evidence, checked URLs and remaining gaps</a></p><details><summary>Show {number(recovered.length)} recovered image contexts and their provenance</summary><div class="detail-table-wrap"><table class="detail-table"><thead><tr><th>Recovered image</th><th>Release</th><th>Evidence and scope</th></tr></thead><tbody>{recovered.map((resource) => { const context = releaseLookup.get(resource.release_ids[0]); return <tr><td><a href={resource.path}>View local image</a><br/><code>{resource.capture_url}</code></td><td>{context && <a href={versionPath(context.project, context.release)}>{context.release.name} {context.release.version}</a>}{resource.release_ids.length > 1 && <span> +{resource.release_ids.length - 1}</span>}</td><td>{scope(resource)}{resource.original_archive && <p><a href={resource.original_archive.url}>Download original GIF</a><br/>Local animated WebP preview{resource.display_transformation.resize && ` (${resource.display_transformation.resize.width}px wide)`}; frame timing preserved.</p>}{resource.source_repository && <p>{resource.source_repository}<br/><code>{resource.source_revision}</code></p>}{resource.phar_entry && <p>{resource.phar_entry}</p>}</td></tr>; })}</tbody></table></div></details></section>
<section id="chrome-recheck" class="detail-section"><h2>Wayback recheck in Chrome</h2><p>On 19 October 2026, {number(chrome.baseline_unavailable)} remaining image contexts were investigated again: {number(chrome.recovered)} recovered and {number(chrome.remaining)} still unavailable. This pass recovered {chrome.original_url_captures} contexts from captures of their original URLs and {chrome.related_url_copies} from a related repository URL, with release-time identity unverified.</p><p>Chrome completed unfiltered CDX lookups for {chrome.url_checks.length} distinct non-Genboy URLs. Two GIFs had been indexed as application/octet-stream, so an image-only MIME filter had hidden them. Compressed SVG responses were decoded before safe rasterization. The two original GIFs are preserved separately in the project's artifact repository; the site serves local animated WebP previews, including a 720px-wide preview of Elevator. Frame counts, delays and loop settings are retained.</p><p><strong>Genboy: {chrome.genboy.contexts} contexts remain unavailable.</strong> The domain-wide CDX index contained {chrome.genboy.indexed_urls} distinct URLs and no matching image files. The saved Festival pages still referenced missing uploads; opening the archived logo returned “The Wayback Machine has not archived that URL.” This establishes the result for the queried index and pages, rather than ruling out copies elsewhere.</p><p><a class="text-link" href={`/data/snapshots/${catalog.pointer.snapshot_id}/media-chrome-audit.json`}>Chrome recheck evidence and all 134 investigated contexts</a> · <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/poggit-archive/artifacts/releases/tag/media-originals-2026-10-19-0001">Original GIFs and checksum manifest</a></p></section>
<section class="detail-section"><h2>Documents and builds</h2><p>The archive preserves 5,020 descriptions, 3,636 changelogs and all 5,021 PHAR manifests. “Preserved document” opens the locally saved original text. Dev Build links open the build IDs and commit recorded for the selected release. The full original Poggit CI interface, historical CI logs and review records were not preserved.</p><p>Normal builds verify and read committed files. They do not request images or release documents from external websites. Site source and media can be copied to another static host.</p></section>
<section id="historical-links" class="detail-section"><h2>Historical and external links</h2><p>Links to captured Poggit plugin versions, downloads, documents and known builds are redirected to their preserved equivalents. This section is the destination for Poggit links with no matching preserved record.</p><p>GitHub profiles, issue trackers, Discord, videos, donation pages and other live services remain optional external references. Their contents were not mirrored. Opening one leaves the archive; merely viewing a plugin page does not contact them.</p><p>All 5,021 plugin PHARs, 259 original/rebuilt virion PHARs, 259 virion source ZIPs and 23 PHAR-derived plugin source ZIPs have same-origin copies. The project's own <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/poggit-archive/artifacts">artifact repository</a> holds backups and the large plugin Git source ZIPs, independently of the authors' repositories and Poggit. Hosting and these remaining ZIP downloads still use GitHub infrastructure. Keeping every source ZIP and PHAR on Pages alongside the site would exceed GitHub Pages' 1 GB site limit.</p></section>
<section class="detail-section"><h2>Unavailable images</h2><p>These records are preservation gaps, with the original URL and last capture error retained for follow-up.</p><details><summary>Show {number(missing.length)} unavailable image contexts</summary><div class="detail-table-wrap"><table class="detail-table"><thead><tr><th>Image source</th><th>Release</th><th>Last result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{missing.map((resource) => { const context = releaseLookup.get(resource.release_ids[0]); return <tr><td><code>{resource.original_url}</code></td><td>{context && <a href={versionPath(context.project, context.release)}>{context.release.name} {context.release.version}</a>}{resource.release_ids.length > 1 && <span> +{resource.release_ids.length - 1}</span>}</td><td>{resource.attempts?.at(-1) || "Not preserved"}</td></tr>; })}</tbody></table></div></details></section>
</main><SiteFooter /></body></html>
